  "changes": [
    "PASSIVE consumes a single caster-owned three-second nimble buff only after a connected enemy basic hit, including shield absorption. E and R refresh the same buff without stacking. Ordinary attacks before completion, skills, zero, immune and friendly contacts do not consume or fabricate it.",
    "Q is one actual piercing fire projectile, one hit per enemy per missile, with no friendly/dead/off-path/cross-duel contact. It follows the existing GGD skill-through-terrain decision in sim/map/lineOfSight.ts. The fire projectile remains a visual proxy, not an accepted original fan model.",
    "W uses the actual caster origin and cast direction for a 120-degree 2.5-unit front arc, one small-tier magic hit per enemy, excluding the rear and out-of-range targets.",
    "E sweeps the real body path through enemies once each and continues to its five-unit endpoint or terrain stop. Generic dash.onTouch/touchScope carries the real cast identity and shared nested-effect bake; only this opt-in continuing dash skips soft unit separation. Walls and static props remain blocking, and death cancels the pending displacement.",
    "R has a 0.65-second interruptible windup, seven-unit first-contact dash, and a primary physical hit. A true HP/shield contact from that cast starts three nearby followups and one 1.8-unit final explosion. Empty casts, wall-only stops and immunity cannot start it; each strike rechecks three-unit range, and death/settled combat cancels pending strikes. No extra invulnerability or control was added.",
    "EX grants a three-second window with at most three followups. Only the caster's actual connected ability hits can produce a 0.1-second delayed hit on the same original victim; each accepted cast counts once across targets/waves. Basics, other casters and proc damage cannot recurse. A lost, dead or distant victim is not replaced.",
    "Generic dash.onEndOn=resolved distinguishes natural distance/terrain/contact completion after nonzero movement from cancellation/replacement. Existing always/completed options remain available for old content. Touch and stop contact modes are rejected when authored together; touchScope without onTouch is rejected.",
    "Hook oncePerCast still requires actual HP damage by default; explicit damageConnected also admits absorbed shield damage. Existing default cast-credit cases and Azazel energy behavior remain in regression.",
    "Editor and shared scenario preparation now allow actual EX before another slot, using the real exSlot/unlock path. It preserves mana, cooldown, damage and state, and does not write setup into the hero. Source snapshots and instantiated projects remain isolated."
  ],
